# MonkeySkills Git Commit Rules

## Branch naming

- Features: `feat/<short-description>`
- Bug fixes: `bugs/<short-description>`
- Never commit directly to `main`, `master`, or `develop`

## Commit message format

```
<type>: <short summary>

<optional body>

<trailer per the commit skill>
```

Follow the `commit` skill's trailer conventions (it defines the exact trailer line); do not hardcode a specific model or assistant name here.

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`

## Workflow

1. Use `/commit` after any MonkeyMode phase — it reads MonkeyMode state and stages the right files
2. One commit per story or logical change unit
3. Push only the current topic branch, never force-push to shared branches
4. Open a PR to the default branch after the full feature is complete
